{"paper": "SSC-CPO-Tier1-28-Jun-2024-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 50, "tagged_count": 50, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Find the natural number obtained when the number 13 is subtracted from the mean proportional of 75 and 12.", "options": [{"text": "14", "added": false}, {"text": "27", "added": false}, {"text": "17", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "The following table shows the classification of 100 students based on the marks obtained by them in Maths and Science in an examination. Find the number of students scoring less than 40% marks in aggregates.", "options": [{"text": "28", "added": false}, {"text": "26", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "22", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "marks-and-exam", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "S drives his car and covers 37 km and 500 m in 90 minutes. What is his average speed (in km/h)?", "options": [{"text": "25", "added": false}, {"text": "20", "added": false}, {"text": "40", "added": false}, {"text": "22.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "average-speed", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "Which of the following statements is/are correct? A. A triangle can have all angles less than 60°. B. A triangle can 