ext of Sanskrit were incorrectly entered as 99 instead of 66. If there are 55 students in the class, then what is the increment in the average marks of the class in Sanskrit because of this typing error?", "options": [{"text": "0.4", "added": false}, {"text": "0.8", "added": false}, {"text": "0.6", "added": false}, {"text": "0.2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "Bhavani spends 68% of her income. Her income increases by 15% and her expenditure increases by 10%. How much is the increase in the percentage of saving? (Use decimal up to 2 digits)", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "One laddoo with a radius of 5 cm belongs to a shopkeeper. How many laddoos of radius 2.5 cm may be created from the same one laddoo?", "options": [{"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "conversion-and-melting", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "Of the three angles of a triangle, one is twice the smallest and another one is thrice the smallest. Find the value of the smallest angle.", "options": [{"text": "65°", "added": false}, {"text": "60°", "added": false}, {"text": "30°", "added": false}, {"text": "45°", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "lines-and-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "32", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}, {"text": "28", "added": false}, {"text": "30", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "Two trains 230 m and 270 m long are running in opposite directions at speeds of 42 km/h and 48 km/h, respectively. They cross each other in:", "options": [{"text": "22 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "20 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "25 seconds", "added": false}, {"text": "30 seconds", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "999", "added": false}, {"text": "995", "added": false}, {"text": "997", "added": false}, {"text": "991", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "A retailer marks up his goods by 130% and offers 25% discount. What will be the selling price (in ₹) if the cost price is ₹ 1600?", "options": [{"text": "2760", "added": false}, {"text": "1980", "added": false}, {"text": "3680", "added": false}, {"text": "1765", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "120", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}, {"text": "100", "added": false}, {"text": "150", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "A boatman rows 2 km in 10 mins, along the stream and 12 km in 2 hours against the stream. What is the speed of the stream?", "options": [{"text": "4 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "3.5 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "3 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "2.5 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "upstream-downstream", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 21, "text": "In an election between two candidates, the candidate who gets 35% of the votes polled is defeated by 15,900 votes. What is the total number of votes polled?", "options": [{"text": "45,000", "added": false}, {"text": "35,000", "added": false}, {"text": "43,000", "added": false}, {"text": "53,000", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 22, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 23, "text": "A boat covers 24 km upstream and 36 km downstream in 10 hours, and 36 km upstream and 24 km downstream in 12 hours. The speed of the current is:", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Boats-Streams", "sub": "upstream-downstream", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 24, "text": "A certain amount of money becomes thrice in 5 years at compound interest. How many years it will take to become 9 times?", "options": [{"text": "15 years", "added": false}, {"text": "10 years", "added": false}, {"text": "8 years", "added": false}, {"text": "25 years", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "ci-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 25, "text": "Simplify [25 - ( - 4){9 - (6 - 2)}] ÷ [3 × {6 + ( - 3) × ( - 3)}].", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 26, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 27, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "500", "added": false}, {"text": "2000", "added": false}, {"text": "1000", "added": false}, {"text": "400", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 28, "text": "In how many years will ₹2,500 be invested at the rate of 12% per annum simple interest, which amounts to ₹4,900?", "options": [{"text": "4", "added": false}, {"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 29, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cone", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 30, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 31, "text": "A shopkeeper buys oranges at the rate of 10 oranges for ₹50 and sells them at the rate of 12 oranges for ₹74. Find his gain or loss percentage.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 32, "text": "The angles of a triangle are in the ratio 1 : 2 : 3, then find the ratio of the corresponding sides.", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "lines-and-angles", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 33, "text": "Find the value of [{(82 + 48 ÷ 8 × 3) + 5 × 6 } – 7.5 × 2].", "options": [{"text": "115", "added": false}, {"text": "125", "added": false}, {"text": "121", "added": false}, {"text": "130", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 34, "text": "A number is first decreased by 10%, then increased by 30% and then further it is decreased by 20%. What is the net decrease percentage in the number?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 35, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "tan2θ", "added": false}, {"text": "tan θ", "added": false}, {"text": "cot2θ", "added": false}, {"text": "cot θ", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "ratios-and-tables", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 36, "text": "Ravi and Sanju together can do a job in 2 days, Sanju and Mahesh can do it in 4 days, while Ravi and Mahesh can do it in 2days. What is the number of days required for Ravi to do the same job alone?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 37, "text": "A seller offers a discount of 12% if the total sale price of different products purchased by a single customer is below ₹3,000, and discount of 15% if the total sale value of all the products exceeds ₹3,000. A shirt costing ₹900 was sold to Anand after earning a margin of 9% and also a jacket costing ₹1,900 was sold to him after a margin of 6%. How much does Anand have to pay (in ₹) for the final settlement of the bill?", "options": [{"text": "2,645.60", "added": false}, {"text": "2,953.60", "added": false}, {"text": "3,005.40", "added": false}, {"text": "2,635.60", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 38, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1625.37 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "1821.47 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "1428.78 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "1527.43 cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 39, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 40, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 41, "text": "The length of the side of a cube is 8 cm. Find the volume of the cube?", "options": [{"text": "664 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "612 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "512 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "564 cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 42, "text": "A reduction of 7.5% in the cost price of a commodity enables a shopkeeper to purchase 15 kg more than what he previously purchased for a sum of ₹7,400. In order to make a profit of 32.5% on the pre-reduction cost price of the commodity, at what price (in ₹) per kg should the commodity be sold?", "options": [{"text": "54", "added": false}, {"text": "52", "added": false}, {"text": "51", "added": false}, {"text": "53", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 43, "text": "A sum of ₹17,600 was divided between Jeevan, Praveen and Kanan, such that the ratio of the sums received by Jeevan and Praveen was 5 : 8, while the ratio of the sums received by Praveen and Kanan was 3 : 2. How much money did Jeevan receive as his share?", "options": [{"text": "₹4,850", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4,750", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4,800", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4,900", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "ratio-basics", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 44, "text": "The following table shows the gross turnover (in crores) of a company over 5 years. By what percentage is the gross turnover of 2020 higher than the gross turnover of 2018?", "options": [{"text": "20%", "added": false}, {"text": "5%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "13%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "basic-percentage", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 45, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "₹4,573", "added": false}, {"text": "₹4,375", "added": false}, {"text": "₹3,745", "added": false}, {"